 "verdict": "SURVIVES on the framework's own moment discipline, with the deep-SPARC lane in 4.2-sigma tension: M1 (a2-moment identity E[g_obs^2] = E[g_bar^2] + a0 E[g_bar]) passes the 5-SE kill bar on every real disk-galaxy ensemble under the honest galaxy-clustered bootstrap (SPARC full 3389 rings z=+1.84; SPARC deep 1152 rings z=+5.65 -- deficit +0.44 x a0E[g_bar], the ring-level z=-10.2 is not the honest one; the deficit maps to a0_eff-deep = 6.8e-11 = 0.73 a0, i.e. it reproduces the committed G208 staircase register (0.69e-10) within 2%); MIGHTEE 80 rings z=+4.28 (positive, no kill; its +0.137 dex deep offset = 1.87x normalization, the G199 MIGHTEE rung); M3 4th-moment identity passes on all disk lanes (+1.39, +0.32, +1.55); the CLASH cluster cross-check fails M3 at z4=+5.03 (cluster-population offset +0.586 dex) and carries an X-correlated residual structure in M2 -- reported, not merged.  Precision conversion: the full-range SPARC ring ensemble resolves the a0-term only at SE/a0E[g_bar] ~ 7.9 (N_req ~ 5.3e6 for a full-size violation); the deep cut (g_bar < 0.2 a0) and MIGHTEE-class deep samples resolve it at 0.07-0.17 (N_req ~ 60-130).  The synthetic twin (4% scatter + 15% misclassification, labeled control-only) is not false-killed (z=+0.63) and its M2 permutation implied-corr test shows no false tension (z_corr=-1.1): the machinery is calibrated on a perfect line before touching real data."
